-- Build flags (redesign build plan 2026-11-13). Features=false hides the Features tab
-- and drops the Feature Egg from the hatch list; saved features keep rendering.
-- DayNight=false (batch 2026-11-13, W1) locks the garden clock to dusk: HollowClock.sample
-- returns the dusk state and the world keeps the WorldDusk lighting and sky.
-- Park=false (Pet Park K1, 2026-11-13) leaves GardenState without a ParkDirector: no playground
-- membership, slots or Play date, and the garden snapshot exactly as before. ON for the private
-- two-account test build (2026-11-13); confirm with Spencer before any public publish.
-- TestFreshSaves (TEST ONLY, Spencer 2026-11-13): true gives each private publish a fresh progress
-- store keyed by PlaceVersion (ProgressStore). v1 launch build (2026-11-17): false, so every
-- save persists in "EggDropLaunchV3" across updates. Never turn it back on in a public build.
-- PseudoLocale=true (v1 track C, text-fit check): UICopy.get returns every string ~35% longer
-- with accented letters in [brackets]. Studio only (UICopy ignores it outside Studio); keep false.
-- SecondPet (overnight 2026-11-14, slice E): the earned pet in collection bit 8 (account id `blip`).
-- ON since 2026-11-19 (v2 Bunny wiring, Sol): the slot now holds the Bunny (BunnyRigDefinition), free on
-- the 7th stamp or adopted for 400 Stars (EarnedPets.Rules). EarnedPets.enabled() also needs the rig.
-- WeeklyShelf=true (slice C): the Monday-reset spotlight shelf with 20% off; false hides it.
-- DeckNet* (deck network rework, artifacts/qa-2026-11-16c-v775/deck-network-plan.md): Ticks stamps the
-- sim tick on board events (S0, presentation data only); Stream sends the owner a 30 Hz snapshot
-- and runs the client clock in shadow (S1); Render draws the deck from it and moves the shared
-- Parts at 8 Hz (S2, needs Stream); Drop answers a tap at once and acks it, with a one-deep server
-- drop queue (S4); Ghost (S5) shows the tapped ball at once and lets the next tap go on its local
-- touch-down (needs Drop; off until verified in Studio). Off = today's path. The server stays authoritative.
-- SimCheck (client-run board B0, artifacts/qa-2026-11-17-v887/B0-plan.md): for the experience creator
-- only (anyone in Studio), the client replays three logged rounds through the shared BoardSim after
-- the loading screen and the server says whether its hashes match (one rail line). Proves a real
-- phone steps the shared sim to the server's bits. No board, save or other player is touched.
-- DeckClientSim (client-run board, B2-plan.md): field rounds run in lockstep on BoardRoundSim, stepped to
-- the owner's reported tick (ClientSimHost / ClientRoundDriver); the deck still draws the server's Parts
-- until B3. Studio only: ServerStorage attribute DeckClientSim = true turns it on at the next round reset.
-- False = today's server-run BoardSimulation.
-- DeckClientSimTesters (2026-11-17): lockstep rounds for Spencer's test accounts only (SimCheck.isOwner), so he
-- can feel the client-run deck on his phone before B4/B5 and the flag flip. Everyone else: today's path.
-- SimCheck off for launch (Spencer 2026-11-17): phone and PC matched the server on v903; the
-- owner-only check has done its job. True again re-runs it for SimCheck.isOwner accounts.
-- Alive* (ALIVE-BUILD-PLAN-2026-11-22): the build ceiling for springs, menu rises, the close plate and the
-- wind; AliveLife (ALIVE-LIFE-BUILD-PLAN-2026-11-22) for the garden life (petals, bubbles, birds, butterflies). Each also needs the beta place or Studio (Alive.PlaceId) and the server's switch (AliveConfig).
-- AliveWindbed (beta 17, WORLD-ALIVE-LOOK 1.3 D): the continuous wind bed; its switch alone is OFF when missing.
-- LevelsMatter (V3-LEVELS-BUILD-PLAN-2026-11-22): the build ceiling for levels, gates, medals and deck juice. Also
-- needs the beta place or Studio (Levels.PlaceId) and the server's switch (LevelsConfig). Missing = off.
-- GardenDash (V3-DASH-BUILD-PLAN-2026-11-22): the build ceiling for the pet race. Also needs the beta place or
-- Studio (Dash.PlaceId) and the server's switches (DashConfig: garden_dash, garden_dash_prizes). Missing = off.
-- AeroWorld (WORLD-PLAN-2026-11-22 section 9): the build ceiling for the client's Frutiger Aero look. Also needs the
